#, no-wrap
msgid "Dressed boxes for the latest version of Samplomatic"
msgstr "Dressed box untuk versi terkini Samplomatic"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dressed boxes"
msgstr "Dressed box"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dressed boxes {#dressed-boxes}"
msgstr "Dressed box {#dressed-boxes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Physical noise mechanisms that occur during the execution of quantum circuits are contextual. When applying operations on disjoint sets of qubits simultaneously, the noise profile of the overall operation might differ from the noise profiles of the constituent parts if they were applied in isolation. Similarly, for operations that ideally commute on the same qubits, the noise profile associated with the individual operations might not commute and could be different altogether if the order of the operations changed. Therefore, protocols for suppressing, mitigating, and correcting noise need to know the context in which it arises.\n"
msgstr "Mekanisme hingar fizikal yang berlaku semasa pelaksanaan litar kuantum bersifat kontekstual. Apabila operasi dikenakan serentak pada set qubit yang tidak bertindih, profil hingar bagi keseluruhan operasi mungkin berbeza daripada profil hingar bagi bahagian-bahagian komponennya jika dikenakan secara berasingan. Begitu juga, bagi operasi yang secara ideal berkomut pada qubit yang sama, profil hingar yang dikaitkan dengan operasi individu mungkin tidak berkomut dan boleh jadi berbeza sama sekali jika susunan operasi diubah. Oleh itu, protokol untuk menyekat, memitigasi dan membetulkan hingar perlu mengetahui konteks di mana hingar itu timbul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic uses box instructions to reason about collections of circuit operations that should be treated as having a stable noise context, and uses annotations on boxes to allow users to declare and configure that intent. Every box is a scope that owns a set of qubits, operations that act on those qubits, and a list of annotations. Samplomatic annotations specify *directives* and *dressings*. Directives specify what to do with the box, for example, twirl the box. Dressings are groups of parameterized gates to add to the left- or right-side of the box, for example, a layer of single qubit gates. The gates in a dressing incorporate gates from the box and operations required to enact directives, such as the following:\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic menggunakan arahan box untuk menaakul tentang koleksi operasi litar yang harus dianggap mempunyai konteks hingar yang stabil, dan menggunakan anotasi pada box supaya pengguna dapat mengisytiharkan dan mengkonfigurasi hasrat tersebut. Setiap box ialah skop yang memiliki satu set qubit, operasi yang bertindak pada qubit tersebut, dan senarai anotasi. Anotasi Samplomatic menentukan *directive* dan *dressing*. Directive menentukan apa yang perlu dilakukan terhadap box, contohnya, melakukan twirl pada box. Dressing ialah kumpulan gate berparameter yang ditambah pada sebelah kiri atau kanan box, contohnya, satu lapisan gate qubit tunggal. Gate dalam dressing menggabungkan gate daripada box dan operasi yang diperlukan untuk melaksanakan directive, seperti yang berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gates in the box that are compatible with and are on the same side as the parameterized gates.\n"
msgstr "Gate dalam box yang serasi dengan dan berada pada sebelah yang sama dengan gate berparameter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirling gates sampled from a set to randomize the box.\n"
msgstr "Gate twirling yang disampel daripada satu set untuk merawakkan box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise injection gates sampled from a Pauli Lindblad map.\n"
msgstr "Gate suntikan hingar yang disampel daripada peta Pauli Lindblad.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "User-specified basis changing gates.\n"
msgstr "Gate pengubahan basis yang ditentukan pengguna.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that directives can alter dressings of other boxes.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa directive boleh mengubah dressing box lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr "Contoh {#example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose we want to twirl the following circuit, adding random Pauli gates before and after the parallel entangling gates that don’t change the logical content of the circuit, but that do change the effective noise model.\n"
msgstr "Andaikan kita mahu melakukan twirl pada litar berikut, dengan menambah gate Pauli rawak sebelum dan selepas gate belitan selari yang tidak mengubah kandungan logik litar, tetapi mengubah model hingar yang berkesan.\n"

